WEBVTT

00:00:17.210 --> 00:00:19.180
Welcome home, Miku-san.

00:00:19.660 --> 00:00:23.010
Taking an intensive course on 
a Saturday? That's just like you.

00:00:23.010 --> 00:00:23.990
Quite commendable!

00:00:24.290 --> 00:00:26.580
No matter how much praise you give, 
you won't get anything from me.

00:00:27.100 --> 00:00:30.080
The new OS should be coming 
out soon, shouldn't it?

00:00:30.880 --> 00:00:32.690
Ask Mama for that.

00:00:33.080 --> 00:00:34.310
Understood.

00:00:34.310 --> 00:00:35.970
Then, I shall ready your bath.

00:00:35.970 --> 00:00:37.940
Your bath. Your bath. Your bath.

00:00:37.940 --> 00:00:40.160
Why do you always want to 
heat up a bath right away?

00:00:49.410 --> 00:00:50.740
That girl...

00:00:51.690 --> 00:00:54.560
I feel like I've seen her somewhere before.

00:01:05.200 --> 00:01:07.160
There is a message from your mother.

00:01:07.160 --> 00:01:10.000
She says that she will be late 
in returning home today.

00:01:10.330 --> 00:01:13.340
Well, that's got nothing to do with me!

00:02:45.510 --> 00:02:51.060
<b>Step 4
"DIY" Means You'll Find It Possible to Feel Comfortable Anywhere</b>

00:02:46.250 --> 00:02:49.050
Is school... No.

00:02:49.730 --> 00:02:51.220
Could you lend me some soy sauce?

00:02:51.780 --> 00:02:53.280
That doesn't sound natural.

00:02:54.070 --> 00:02:55.140
Oh!

00:02:55.140 --> 00:02:56.980
Can you give me some sasadango?

00:02:56.980 --> 00:02:57.930
Purin-chan?

00:03:00.580 --> 00:03:02.200
Hello.

00:03:02.910 --> 00:03:05.430
H-Hello.

00:03:05.430 --> 00:03:08.460
Your mama is working the
 night shift today, isn't she?

00:03:09.950 --> 00:03:12.680
Oh, um, yes.

00:03:13.880 --> 00:03:16.720
I'll prepare dinner right away, all right?

00:03:16.720 --> 00:03:17.660
What?

00:03:19.520 --> 00:03:21.100
I'm home!

00:03:24.210 --> 00:03:26.470
Oh, welcome, Purin!

00:03:26.730 --> 00:03:29.610
It's been a long time since 
you came to hang out!

00:03:29.610 --> 00:03:32.250
I-I didn't come to hang out.

00:03:32.250 --> 00:03:34.060
I came to ask you to give 
me some sasadango...

00:03:34.670 --> 00:03:35.960
No, that's not it!

00:03:36.310 --> 00:03:40.240
Jobko-chan, this is Purin. 
You can call her Pudding.

00:03:40.240 --> 00:03:41.600
Who's "Pudding"?

00:03:42.130 --> 00:03:43.720
I am Puri—

00:03:44.560 --> 00:03:47.490
Miku. Suride Miku.

00:03:47.490 --> 00:03:49.400
Nice to meet you.

00:03:49.400 --> 00:03:54.430
This is Juliet Queen 
Elizabeth VIII, Jobko-chan!

00:03:54.840 --> 00:03:56.450
Jobko-chan?

00:03:58.170 --> 00:03:59.430
A pleasure.

00:03:59.950 --> 00:04:01.890
Juliet...

00:04:01.890 --> 00:04:05.050
Queen Elizabeth VIII...

00:04:05.500 --> 00:04:08.610
The man who's called a 
supernova in the IT field...

00:04:08.610 --> 00:04:11.570
That super-genius specialist?! 
You're his daughter?!

00:04:12.180 --> 00:04:14.330
Wh-Why...?

00:04:14.810 --> 00:04:16.660
Okay, thank you for waiting!

00:04:16.660 --> 00:04:19.600
Saltimbocca! A pork version!

00:04:20.270 --> 00:04:22.860
Yay! I love it!

00:04:23.160 --> 00:04:24.550
Thank you for the meal.

00:04:25.640 --> 00:04:30.130
<i>Why is the only daughter of the CTO of a 
company with globally cutting-edge tech...</i>

00:04:30.130 --> 00:04:31.900
<i>doing an exchange program at Gata Girls'?</i>

00:04:31.900 --> 00:04:34.230
Yum, it's delicious!

00:04:34.230 --> 00:04:37.360
Saltimbocca, pork version!

00:04:47.200 --> 00:04:48.520
It's delicious.

00:04:52.150 --> 00:04:54.340
It works really well as a pork dish.

00:04:58.990 --> 00:05:01.090
Thank you for the meal.

00:05:28.330 --> 00:05:30.820
Purin, did you like the food?

00:05:34.510 --> 00:05:35.610
Yeah.

00:05:38.730 --> 00:05:39.870
What?

00:05:39.870 --> 00:05:42.520
You wrote it wrong on the application? 
That's why you're at Gata Girls'?

00:05:42.520 --> 00:05:45.920
I was actually supposed to do 
my exchange courses at YuuVoc.

00:05:45.920 --> 00:05:50.280
I wanted to study cutting-edge 
industrial technologies and theories.

00:05:46.240 --> 00:05:50.280
<u>Gata</u>gata Girls' High School

00:05:46.240 --> 00:05:50.280
<u>Yuyu</u> Girls' Vocational High School

00:05:46.240 --> 00:05:50.280
Cutting-edge

00:05:51.440 --> 00:05:54.690
So, what kinds of courses 
are you taking there now?

00:05:55.400 --> 00:05:59.280
Today I had an intensive course 
on the future of deep learning.

00:05:59.280 --> 00:06:00.120
I see.

00:06:00.520 --> 00:06:04.090
So, basically, when AI 
gains true self-awareness,

00:06:04.090 --> 00:06:07.470
there will be a paradigm shift 
in humanity's awareness.

00:06:07.470 --> 00:06:11.400
Yes, through the technological singularity, 
humanity's various problems,

00:06:10.970 --> 00:06:14.220
These sasadango for 
dessert are really yummy!

00:06:11.400 --> 00:06:16.310
like those caused by differing philosophies or
 language barriers, will be resolved all at once.

00:06:15.930 --> 00:06:18.150
The bath is ready!

00:06:18.610 --> 00:06:20.150
Okay!

00:06:20.150 --> 00:06:22.730
Jobko-chan, you can go first.

00:06:23.040 --> 00:06:24.320
For a bath?

00:06:25.010 --> 00:06:26.490
Are you staying the night?

00:06:26.490 --> 00:06:29.540
Oh, did you want to take one 
after you get back to the hotel?

00:06:31.500 --> 00:06:34.290
Well, I guess I'll head home now.

00:06:42.330 --> 00:06:44.590
This bathroom is cramped.

00:06:44.770 --> 00:06:47.700
Then you should have used 
the one at the hotel.

00:06:47.700 --> 00:06:49.960
I don't like being alone.

00:06:50.990 --> 00:06:53.680
Then why would you do an exchange program?

00:06:57.660 --> 00:06:59.550
Oh! So, um...

00:06:59.940 --> 00:07:01.780
What we were talking about earlier...

00:07:01.780 --> 00:07:04.720
I think nanocarbons still have a lot of potential,

00:07:04.720 --> 00:07:08.630
like accelerating CPUs and 
extending battery life.

00:07:09.540 --> 00:07:11.190
Yes, I agree.

00:07:11.630 --> 00:07:17.430
Carbon nanotubes still haven't reached 
the true potential of their...

00:07:14.320 --> 00:07:18.370
Purin and Jobko-chan seem to speak 
the same language, don't they?

00:07:18.670 --> 00:07:20.780
That's great! I'm so glad!

00:07:23.750 --> 00:07:26.080
Your strategy is to make 
the club room cuter?

00:07:26.080 --> 00:07:29.410
Yeah. In order to keep the DIY club going,

00:07:29.410 --> 00:07:32.140
we have to get more members, you see?

00:07:32.400 --> 00:07:37.260
DIY is moldy, outdated, 
useless, and illogical.

00:07:37.260 --> 00:07:39.720
Jobko-chan said exactly the same thing!

00:07:40.510 --> 00:07:44.680
Wait. Was it Jobko-chan who 
said the same thing as Purin?

00:07:45.890 --> 00:07:46.720
Huh?

00:07:47.470 --> 00:07:50.140
So, did you get more members?

00:07:50.140 --> 00:07:52.020
Not at all.

00:07:52.580 --> 00:07:56.460
We made our sign cuter, 
and we made a bench, but...

00:07:56.850 --> 00:07:59.960
Maybe it still isn't cute enough?

00:08:01.540 --> 00:08:03.920
Wow, that looks delicious!

00:08:08.480 --> 00:08:11.200
To get members that way and having 
lots of snacks at the same time...

00:08:11.200 --> 00:08:12.530
It's just impossible, understand?

00:08:12.980 --> 00:08:13.760
Huh?

00:08:17.030 --> 00:08:20.380
I know exactly how you think.

00:08:21.260 --> 00:08:23.150
Wow, that's amazing, Purin!

00:08:24.700 --> 00:08:26.140
I'm going to go home now.

00:08:26.620 --> 00:08:28.640
I have assignments to finish.

00:08:29.060 --> 00:08:31.270
You should just stay the night.

00:08:31.270 --> 00:08:32.890
Why would I stay here?

00:08:33.520 --> 00:08:35.060
You used to all the time before.

00:08:35.580 --> 00:08:40.330
I'm allergic to cats and dogs 
and pigs and you, Serufu!

00:08:41.850 --> 00:08:43.700
Oh, that's right.

00:08:44.440 --> 00:08:45.260
Idiot.

00:08:58.660 --> 00:09:01.340
Miku-san, the bath is ready.

00:09:01.680 --> 00:09:03.750
I've already had one today.

00:09:04.320 --> 00:09:06.050
Have you? I see.

00:09:06.620 --> 00:09:08.720
Why do you sound so disappointed?

00:09:09.430 --> 00:09:11.950
By the way, on the topic of my OS...

00:09:11.950 --> 00:09:13.230
Good night.

00:09:15.070 --> 00:09:17.570
Yes, good night.

00:09:32.250 --> 00:09:33.520
Good morning.

00:09:34.020 --> 00:09:35.050
Huh?

00:09:38.080 --> 00:09:39.130
What?

00:09:39.560 --> 00:09:41.220
How did you get in here?

00:09:41.220 --> 00:09:45.810
Disabling the security system on your 
front door was very easy for me.

00:09:46.330 --> 00:09:48.230
And the computer password?

00:09:48.230 --> 00:09:51.050
It's like it didn't even exist for me.

00:09:53.510 --> 00:09:55.190
Very impressive, YuuVoc.

00:09:55.190 --> 00:09:58.060
This content is exactly what 
I'd hoped it would be.

00:09:58.060 --> 00:10:01.560
And the texts are prepared in a 
number of different languages.

00:10:01.850 --> 00:10:02.910
Good job.

00:10:03.260 --> 00:10:05.040
This is no time to be saying "good job"!

00:10:05.270 --> 00:10:06.840
Disable file protection...

00:10:07.180 --> 00:10:08.280
and copy!

00:10:08.900 --> 00:10:10.280
Copy?!

00:10:10.280 --> 00:10:13.140
Jobko-san, your request has been completed.

00:10:13.140 --> 00:10:14.290
Thank you.

00:10:14.290 --> 00:10:15.540
What request?!

00:10:16.010 --> 00:10:18.100
Wait... "Jobko-san"?

00:10:18.100 --> 00:10:19.300
You've registered her as an owner?

00:10:19.300 --> 00:10:20.830
It's no problem.

00:10:20.830 --> 00:10:22.840
I'm controlling him using my card.

00:10:23.390 --> 00:10:27.260
Oh. And I went ahead and installed 
"happy dance" while I was at it.

00:10:32.570 --> 00:10:34.270
Hey, Serufu!

00:10:34.770 --> 00:10:37.810
How long has it been since 
I've been in Purin's room?

00:10:38.890 --> 00:10:40.750
More importantly...

00:10:40.750 --> 00:10:42.660
why is this girl in my house?!

00:10:42.660 --> 00:10:46.590
Yesterday, you and Jobko-chan had 
a lot of fun talking, right?

00:10:46.900 --> 00:10:50.380
W-We did... but that's not the point!

00:10:50.900 --> 00:10:53.350
Arrival is imminent.

00:10:59.450 --> 00:11:03.310
There's so much. What did you order?

00:11:03.840 --> 00:11:05.360
No idea.

00:11:06.060 --> 00:11:07.390
Collapsible Saw 
with Replaceable Blade

00:11:06.180 --> 00:11:07.390
Water-Based Polyurethane

00:11:06.310 --> 00:11:08.680
Acrylic Cord

00:11:06.810 --> 00:11:10.440
Japanese Industrial Standard
 Heavy Duty Nippers

00:11:07.590 --> 00:11:09.450
Yes, it's all here.

00:11:07.600 --> 00:11:10.440
14.4V Rechargeable Power Drill/Driver

00:11:08.770 --> 00:11:10.440
Hinoki Lumber 4cm x 6cm x 70cm

00:11:09.180 --> 00:11:10.440
Stainless Steel Screws,
 Slim, Coarse Thread 3.8 (70)

00:11:10.430 --> 00:11:12.350
Let's get started!

00:11:13.950 --> 00:11:16.200
Starting today, I'll be living here.

00:11:16.540 --> 00:11:17.380
What?

00:11:29.080 --> 00:11:30.830
Living here?!

00:11:30.830 --> 00:11:33.800
Yes. I'm sick of living at the hotel.

00:11:33.800 --> 00:11:35.160
You decided without asking?!

00:11:35.160 --> 00:11:37.190
It's only for the first term.

00:11:37.190 --> 00:11:39.660
And, of course, I'll pay for food and rent.

00:11:39.960 --> 00:11:43.760
Oh, that means we'll be able to go 
to school together, Jobko-chan!

00:11:43.760 --> 00:11:45.670
Don't just accept this!

00:11:47.610 --> 00:11:50.990
It's just the right width 
to hang a hammock.

00:11:50.990 --> 00:11:52.740
A hammock?

00:11:52.970 --> 00:11:55.230
Will you weave one for me, Pudding?

00:11:55.230 --> 00:11:56.670
My name is Puri—

00:11:58.140 --> 00:12:00.370
What app is that?

00:12:00.370 --> 00:12:03.140
This app hasn't been released yet.

00:12:03.140 --> 00:12:06.050
It uses AI to assess the space 
and determine the optimal—

00:12:08.950 --> 00:12:13.550
If you help me, I wouldn't mind 
installing it on your tablet, Pudding.

00:12:15.950 --> 00:12:17.120
Hmph!

00:12:17.120 --> 00:12:21.270
There are other brand-new, 
freshly-minted apps in here, too!

00:12:23.390 --> 00:12:25.000
Oh, all right, fine!

00:12:25.430 --> 00:12:27.350
Then, I'll leave it to you.

00:12:27.350 --> 00:12:28.920
It's easy!

00:12:32.510 --> 00:12:34.920
Take this and go like this here...

00:12:34.920 --> 00:12:37.240
And if those are combined like this...

00:12:38.300 --> 00:12:41.460
Yes, they should just fit in that corner.

00:12:41.930 --> 00:12:46.020
Say, Jobko-chan? Is there 
anything I can help with?

00:12:46.020 --> 00:12:51.370
Well, could you bring the tools and 
materials up here to the balcony?

00:12:51.370 --> 00:12:52.750
Leave it to me!

00:12:53.510 --> 00:12:56.650
And by repeating these steps, 
you can make a hammock.

00:12:53.580 --> 00:12:54.780
Yeah!

00:12:56.650 --> 00:12:58.170
Wow...

00:13:02.360 --> 00:13:03.430
Serufu?!

00:13:03.720 --> 00:13:06.500
Ow...

00:13:06.820 --> 00:13:09.920
Serufu is a Japanese klutz.

00:13:14.700 --> 00:13:16.810
Thanks, Purin.

00:13:17.270 --> 00:13:19.180
Really, you were like this way back then...

00:13:20.800 --> 00:13:22.820
and you haven't changed a bit, have you?

00:13:21.850 --> 00:13:22.820
Ow!

00:13:24.050 --> 00:13:27.090
Come on. We should get this 
done before nightfall.

00:13:28.420 --> 00:13:30.040
Yes, we should.

00:13:33.080 --> 00:13:34.820
Wow...

00:13:53.780 --> 00:13:55.850
You're pretty good at that, aren't you?

00:13:56.260 --> 00:13:58.700
This much is nothing.

00:13:58.700 --> 00:14:00.280
Unlike Serufu,

00:14:00.280 --> 00:14:02.490
I'm fairly deft at things.

00:14:03.150 --> 00:14:08.910
<b>Patience</b>

00:14:03.150 --> 00:14:08.910
<b>Through the Way 
of the Ninja, 
a Certain Peace</b>

00:14:04.020 --> 00:14:08.330
Serufu has always been clumsy, 
so she got injured all the time.

00:14:08.910 --> 00:14:11.870
That's why I did the handiwork for her.

00:14:12.670 --> 00:14:15.480
Even now, she'll quickly get distracted

00:14:15.480 --> 00:14:16.960
and end up injured.

00:14:18.350 --> 00:14:19.730
I see.

00:14:23.290 --> 00:14:26.540
Never mind. Only a little left to do.

00:14:27.990 --> 00:14:28.760
Yeah.

00:14:32.540 --> 00:14:33.330
Oh!

00:14:34.070 --> 00:14:35.840
The last one!

00:14:38.230 --> 00:14:40.230
<b>Patience</b>

00:14:41.120 --> 00:14:43.030
We're done!

00:14:43.700 --> 00:14:45.150
Perfect!

00:14:45.150 --> 00:14:46.930
That's Jobko-chan for you!

00:14:46.930 --> 00:14:49.810
I can tell how much you love DIY!

00:14:51.880 --> 00:14:54.340
"Good job," you say?

00:14:55.310 --> 00:14:57.350
It's not a good job at all.

00:14:58.340 --> 00:15:00.290
I ended up helping,

00:15:00.810 --> 00:15:02.500
but I'm sure that all of this...

00:15:03.880 --> 00:15:05.940
will make Mama angry.

00:15:06.780 --> 00:15:08.200
I'm home!

00:15:13.360 --> 00:15:17.370
So... that's what's going on...

00:15:17.370 --> 00:15:19.950
and, um...

00:15:20.150 --> 00:15:21.870
You're going to live here?

00:15:22.160 --> 00:15:25.110
Yes. A homestay.

00:15:25.560 --> 00:15:28.270
A homestay? This girl?

00:15:29.990 --> 00:15:31.230
Yes.

00:15:33.570 --> 00:15:34.710
That's fine.

00:15:35.030 --> 00:15:36.120
It is?!

00:15:36.480 --> 00:15:39.460
But we will receive that 
which is ours to receive.

00:15:39.460 --> 00:15:42.510
Food and rent for a month...

00:15:42.510 --> 00:15:43.630
Let's see.

00:15:44.570 --> 00:15:45.620
Ten thousand.

00:15:45.850 --> 00:15:48.500
Ten thousand... dollars?

00:15:49.240 --> 00:15:50.120
Okay!

00:15:50.340 --> 00:15:53.170
What? Wait, Mama, I think 
that's a little too...

00:15:53.170 --> 00:15:55.260
I won't budge an inch on the amount.

00:15:55.260 --> 00:15:57.100
Exactly ten thousand yen.

00:15:57.410 --> 00:15:58.350
That's so cheap.

00:15:59.380 --> 00:16:01.550
Thank you, Pudding's mom!

00:16:03.890 --> 00:16:05.510
And with that decided,

00:16:05.510 --> 00:16:07.470
let's celebrate your moving in with a meal.

00:16:07.470 --> 00:16:09.340
Is there anything you want to eat?

00:16:09.340 --> 00:16:11.950
I want to try eating the 
thing called "ohagi"!

00:16:12.210 --> 00:16:13.410
Okay!

00:16:20.460 --> 00:16:22.570
It tastes good!

00:16:31.170 --> 00:16:32.720
Hey, Jobko-chan.

00:16:33.190 --> 00:16:37.550
Why didn't you choose to stay 
at my house instead of Serufu's?

00:16:41.740 --> 00:16:46.090
Because, Pudding, you can teach 
me the YuuVoc curriculum.

00:16:46.090 --> 00:16:50.540
And, Pudding, you can use the 
apps and technology I have.

00:16:50.540 --> 00:16:51.610
It's win-win.

00:16:53.160 --> 00:16:57.960
In Japanese, you have the phrase 
"earning a lot with one stone," right?

00:16:57.960 --> 00:16:59.740
It's "two birds with one stone."

00:17:00.540 --> 00:17:02.330
And the meaning doesn't really apply here.

00:17:03.610 --> 00:17:07.060
You were just lonely staying at 
the hotel by yourself, right?

00:17:08.660 --> 00:17:10.810
That's not it at all.

00:17:11.260 --> 00:17:12.490
You know it is.

00:17:13.540 --> 00:17:20.280
Well, it might not be 
entirely not that... maybe.

00:17:20.280 --> 00:17:21.180
See?

00:17:21.690 --> 00:17:22.870
But...

00:17:23.290 --> 00:17:24.210
But?

00:17:25.240 --> 00:17:29.280
Pudding, I feel like you 
and I are sort of alike.

00:17:29.660 --> 00:17:30.560
What?

00:17:31.640 --> 00:17:33.820
Never mind.

00:17:36.410 --> 00:17:37.610
Jobko-chan?

00:17:38.690 --> 00:17:40.770
Wait. Hey.

00:17:44.140 --> 00:17:47.530
She falls asleep easily. 
What is she, a child?

00:17:53.010 --> 00:17:55.170
A child?

00:17:57.610 --> 00:17:58.750
Good night.

00:18:05.280 --> 00:18:08.060
Here, Purin-chan! I'll give this to you!

00:18:08.660 --> 00:18:10.230
Are you sure?

00:18:10.230 --> 00:18:11.160
Yeah!

00:18:11.440 --> 00:18:15.390
I worked really hard to make it, 
so I want you to have it, Purin-chan!

00:18:15.740 --> 00:18:18.730
I made most of it though...

00:18:18.730 --> 00:18:20.850
I did the finishing touches!

00:18:23.110 --> 00:18:26.130
Thank you. I'll treasure it.

00:18:27.270 --> 00:18:30.200
Then I'll give you the one 
I made, Serufu-chan!

00:18:30.830 --> 00:18:32.180
Thanks!

00:18:44.450 --> 00:18:45.670
Serufu-chan?

00:18:46.670 --> 00:18:48.010
Serufu-chan!

00:18:52.300 --> 00:18:53.900
A secret hideout!

00:18:54.390 --> 00:18:56.240
A secret hideout?

00:18:56.990 --> 00:18:59.960
I was just thinking I'd like 
to build one. Up in a tree!

00:19:00.440 --> 00:19:04.400
And I'd hang this wind chime there.

00:19:26.590 --> 00:19:28.700
Where is Pudding's mom?

00:19:30.080 --> 00:19:32.350
She went to work early this morning.

00:19:46.850 --> 00:19:50.550
Say... What about a tree house?

00:19:51.300 --> 00:19:53.010
A tree house?

00:19:53.010 --> 00:19:55.910
The plan to get more 
members for the DIY club.

00:19:57.500 --> 00:19:59.670
It would probably be a lot of work...

00:19:59.670 --> 00:20:00.770
but it would attract attention.

00:20:02.260 --> 00:20:03.940
Really?

00:20:07.110 --> 00:20:08.200
Let's go.

00:20:16.030 --> 00:20:17.490
From tweed?

00:20:17.490 --> 00:20:18.790
No, a tree house.

00:20:18.790 --> 00:20:21.570
A landmark for the DIY club.

00:20:21.820 --> 00:20:24.900
Oh, a tree house!

00:20:25.920 --> 00:20:29.580
Hmm, a tree house, huh?

00:20:30.520 --> 00:20:32.300
Wow...

00:20:39.740 --> 00:20:41.640
<i>I wonder if she still has it.</i>

00:20:47.940 --> 00:20:50.760
T-Tree... house...

00:20:50.760 --> 00:20:52.690
A tree house?

00:20:52.690 --> 00:20:54.360
It's a great idea, don't you think?

00:20:54.360 --> 00:20:56.700
I just know we'll get lots of members!

00:20:56.920 --> 00:20:59.310
Jobko-chan thought of it for us!

00:20:59.880 --> 00:21:02.070
Not me. Pudding.

00:21:02.390 --> 00:21:05.580
We can do it, can't we? 
Club leader? Takumin?

00:21:06.010 --> 00:21:08.150
I think it would be lovely.

00:21:08.150 --> 00:21:11.000
B-But will we really be able to build one?

00:21:11.480 --> 00:21:12.530
We will.

00:21:12.740 --> 00:21:13.520
What?

00:21:14.590 --> 00:21:15.990
I want to try building it.

00:21:16.720 --> 00:21:20.020
See? Jobko-chan's saying so, too!

00:21:20.660 --> 00:21:21.700
Hmm...

00:21:23.080 --> 00:21:26.430
I think it'll be a little tough 
to get all the materials...

00:21:26.930 --> 00:21:28.520
but I think it's doable.

00:21:28.990 --> 00:21:30.500
Wow!

00:21:30.840 --> 00:21:32.780
Then, let's get started right away!

00:21:32.780 --> 00:21:35.250
I-I'd like it to be cute!

00:21:35.250 --> 00:21:37.190
Okay. Let's go...

00:21:37.190 --> 00:21:38.550
build a tree house!

00:21:40.900 --> 00:21:42.010
Do it...

00:21:42.010 --> 00:21:43.920
Yourself!

00:21:54.070 --> 00:21:55.580
Hi, there!

00:21:58.320 --> 00:21:59.610
A ninja!

00:22:02.070 --> 00:22:04.220
I came to play, meow!

00:23:36.020 --> 00:23:39.970
<b>Step 5</b>

00:23:36.020 --> 00:23:39.970
<b>"DIY" Means Finding a Place to Belong... Finally</b>
